// The first time in Tidewell: the harbour town at the end of the south,
// the lighthouse, and Noor, who knows everybody's business.

## The harbour

::bg{location="tidewell" time="day"}
::music{playback="start" mood="upbeat" volume="normal"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: Tidewell: blue shutters, wet cobbles, nets drying on every railing, and the lighthouse on its rock at the mouth of the harbour, turning even in daylight.
::actor{character="tidewellNoor" anchor="center" action="enter"}
@tidewellNoor{code="0010" emotion="smug"}: You came over the bridge? Then you beat all five and turned down the nice man at the end. Everybody does. He's been there a month.
@tidewellNoor{code="0020"}: I'm Noor. My sister runs the gym. She'll be in the pool. She's always in the pool. You'll know her; she's the one going faster than the water.
@tidewellNoor{code="0030"}: The fishing pier is south, the lighthouse is Isla's, and the cape is past the cliffs, where the weird researcher lives. Don't touch his boats.
::actor{character="tidewellNoor" action="exit"}
